  "title": "Workload Capture Request Schemas Renamed (Breaking)",
  "summary": "The request body schemas for Cloud SQL's Workload Capture methods (start, startReplay, stop, stopReplay) have been renamed. This is a breaking change requiring updates to client code.",
  "details": "The request body schemas used by the `workloadCaptures.start`, `workloadCaptures.startReplay`, `workloadCaptures.stop`, and `workloadCaptures.stopReplay` methods have undergone a breaking rename. Previously, these methods expected request bodies named `SqlWorkloadCapturesStartRequest`, `SqlWorkloadCapturesStartReplayRequest`, `SqlWorkloadCapturesStopRequest`, and `SqlWorkloadCapturesStopReplayRequest` respectively. These schemas have been removed and replaced with new schemas named `WorkloadCapturesStartRequest`, `WorkloadCapturesStartReplayRequest`, `WorkloadCapturesStopRequest`, and `WorkloadCapturesStopReplayRequest`. Developers must update their client code to use the new request body types when calling these Workload Capture methods.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
